IV Curve Tester carrier r0 - static 16-channel load scan

* User-adjustable DUT and front-end assumptions.
* SOURCE_MODE=0: Thevenin source, VOC in series with RSRC.
* SOURCE_MODE=1: equivalent Norton source, VOC/RSRC in parallel with RSRC.
.param SOURCE_MODE=0
.param VOC=3.3
.param RSRC=22
.param RON=6
.param VADC_SUPPLY=3.3
.param ADC_RSER=1k
.param ADC_RIN=10Meg
.param ADC_CIN=5p
.param RESISTOR_RATING=0.25

* Draft nominal load bank from CONNECTION_MATRIX.md.
.param RCH0=1Meg
.param RCH1=20k
.param RCH2=8.2k
.param RCH3=4.3k
.param RCH4=2.2k
.param RCH5=1k
.param RCH6=750
.param RCH7=470
.param RCH8=330
.param RCH9=220
.param RCH10=150
.param RCH11=100
.param RCH12=82
.param RCH13=51
.param RCH14=30
.param RCH15=18

* The ADC model is intentionally simple: 1 kohm sense lead, 10 Mohm
* input resistance, 5 pF placeholder capacitance, and rail clamps.
VADC vdd 0 {VADC_SUPPLY}
.model DCLAMP D(Is=1e-15 N=1 Rs=1 Cjo=1p)

* Each block is an independent replica of the same DUT.  This is equivalent
* to a static one-channel-at-a-time MUX scan; it does not model switch timing.

* Channel 0 / S1 / 1 Mohm
VTH0 th0 0 {VOC*(1-SOURCE_MODE)}
RTH0 th0 dut0 {RSRC + SOURCE_MODE*1e12}
IN0 0 dut0 dc {SOURCE_MODE*VOC/RSRC}
RN0 dut0 0 {RSRC + (1-SOURCE_MODE)*1e12}
RLOAD0 dut0 mux0 {RCH0}
VMEAS0 mux0 ron0 0
RRON0 ron0 0 {RON}
RADC_SER0 dut0 adc0 {ADC_RSER}
RADC_IN0 adc0 0 {ADC_RIN}
CADC0 adc0 0 {ADC_CIN}
DADC_HI0 adc0 vdd DCLAMP
DADC_LO0 0 adc0 DCLAMP

* Channel 1 / S2 / 20 kohm
VTH1 th1 0 {VOC*(1-SOURCE_MODE)}
RTH1 th1 dut1 {RSRC + SOURCE_MODE*1e12}
IN1 0 dut1 dc {SOURCE_MODE*VOC/RSRC}
RN1 dut1 0 {RSRC + (1-SOURCE_MODE)*1e12}
RLOAD1 dut1 mux1 {RCH1}
VMEAS1 mux1 ron1 0
RRON1 ron1 0 {RON}
RADC_SER1 dut1 adc1 {ADC_RSER}
RADC_IN1 adc1 0 {ADC_RIN}
CADC1 adc1 0 {ADC_CIN}
DADC_HI1 adc1 vdd DCLAMP
DADC_LO1 0 adc1 DCLAMP

* Channel 2 / S3 / 8.2 kohm
VTH2 th2 0 {VOC*(1-SOURCE_MODE)}
RTH2 th2 dut2 {RSRC + SOURCE_MODE*1e12}
